### 1. Direct Answer
A blowout preventer (BOP) is a device attached to the wellhead or tree that allows the well to be closed in with or without a string of pipe or wireline in the borehole.

### 2. Technical Explanation
The blowout preventer is a critical piece of equipment used in drilling operations to prevent uncontrolled flows of well fluids or formation fluids from the wellbore. It is typically installed at the wellhead and can be used to close in the well in emergency situations, such as a blowout.

### 3. Supporting Evidence
The definition of a blowout preventer is provided in the API RP 54 document, page 9, which is a standard for drilling safety. This definition is supported by other sections of the document, which provide guidelines for the use and maintenance of blowout preventers.

### 4. Source Citations
The definition of a blowout preventer is cited from the API RP 54 document, page 9 (API RP 54, 3.1.7).

