According to the provided API standard, in the event of a blowout preventer failure, certain safety protocols should be followed. 

When a blowout preventer is used, a rotating head may be used on the blowout preventer assembly with an appropriate working pressure. Additionally, the blooey and bleed-off lines should be a minimum length or equivalent safety measures should be taken, and these lines should be laid from the wellbore as straight and free of sags as practicable and be securely anchored.

In gas drilling operations, a shut-off valve should be installed on the main feeder line. Furthermore, all equipment should be pressure tested before use, and all flowback iron shall be certified/recertified annually using nondestructive testing.

It is also important to note that a full-opening, quick-closing valve should be installed at the top of the kelly to contain formation pressures in the drill string, and there should be two valves installed in the standpipe to control the air or gas supply to the borehole.

Based on available sources, the following information was found. Additional verification may be required.

